## Context
DESIGN-V2 §4 PR-11 and PR-12, honoring D5, with the query critique's repairs.
PR-11 (after #19): the query compiler — quoted phrases and NOT/AND as hard
filters, bare terms soft OR. Phrases evaluate per passage (FTS5-native); AND
and NOT evaluate at ENTRY scope (one MATCH per hard term, id-lists joined on
the hit unit) — passage-scope AND on a multi-chunk entry silently kills
legitimate hits (critique M1). Memory-backend parity via a fold-only,
UNFILTERED token stream (the retained tokenize() arrays are stopword-stripped
— "war and peace" would match "war versus peace"; critique M2), predicate
pushed inside search() before its top-k slice. Failing test: "general
equilibrium" retrieves either-word today. X4 (0025) supplies the
constrained-MATCH ladder constant via json_each (carray does not exist in
node:sqlite — verified).
PR-12: fraction-weighted RRF k=60 behind a flag — v1's rejection overturned by
verified arithmetic (FTS5 clamps idf; all four seams strictly positive;
frac in [0,1] bounds every contribution by plain RRF). Seam invariant
("every ranked list higher-better, strictly positive") as a unit test; golden
Jaccard vs plain-RRF in the PR body (gate thresholds in 0026).

## Exit criteria
- [ ] phrase/AND/NOT per D5 on both backends, entry-scope join, parity stream unfiltered
- [ ] X4's measured threshold in the ladder, not an adjective
- [ ] fraction-RRF flagged, seam-invariant test, golden numbers in the body
- [ ] PRs opened upstream; outcomes recorded here
